  "reflection": "Earlier register readback checks proved digital communication, not analog adoption of the code. The direct old-firmware comparison and a fixed-wiring single-variable test should have been done sooner. Do not attribute this reproduced failure to soldering or a dead DAC.",
  "recovery": "A DAC soft reset restores operation after the reproduced latched condition; repeated DATA, powerdown/enable, SYNC clear and LDAC did not. A reset can transiently restore the M-device midpoint, so no automatic reset was added to normal muted initialization. Plan recovery with outputs disconnected/controlled or a known clean power-up before deployment.",
